  <h2 id="govt-defense">PCM routes into government, defense, and public sector jobs</h2>

  <p>
    Many families associate PCM with only private engineering or NEET.
    The government and defence sector provides serious career routes for PCM students that are often underexplored.
  </p>

  <div class="grid-two">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Defense and armed forces</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>NDA (National Defence Academy):</strong> Entry into the Army, Navy, and Air Force through a UPSC-conducted exam. PCM is mandatory for Air Force and Navy technical branches. Entry salary ₹15–25 LPA all-in with non-monetary benefits. One of the most structured and respected career routes in India for PCM students who want the defense identity.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical Entry Scheme (TES):</strong> Direct entry into the Army as a Short Service Commissioned Officer through 10+2 PCM marks (no written exam). Training at OTA followed by regular service.</li>
        <li><strong>Air Force AFCAT:</strong> Entry into the Air Force's technical, flying, and ground duty branches. Requires PCM and clearing the AFCAT exam.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Research and public sector units</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>ISRO and DRDO:</strong> Scientist/Engineer-B posts are filled through ISRO Centralised Recruitment Board and DRDO exams. Both recruit engineering graduates with strong PCM foundations.</li>
        <li><strong>PSUs (Public Sector Undertakings):</strong> BHEL, ONGC, NTPC, IOCL, and GAIL recruit through GATE scores. A GATE-qualified B.Tech can lead to stable government-sector engineering roles at ₹8–15 LPA + perks.</li>
        <li><strong>Merchant Navy:</strong> B.Sc Nautical Science or Marine Engineering after PCM. Entry-level deck officers and engineers earn ₹3–5 LPA onshore; at sea, the earning potential is significantly higher (₹6–15 LPA tax-free for some ranks).</li>
        <li><strong>Indian Engineering Services (IES):</strong> Technical civil service exam for engineers across civil, electrical, mechanical, and electronics branches. Entry at ₹15–20 LPA with grade-based growth.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Government and PSU routes often get ignored because the preparation period is longer and less glamorous than startup or product company hiring. But the stability, lifetime earnings including benefits, and job security make them worth comparing seriously, not dismissing by default.
  </p>

